艾米·亚当斯就是那个“包包女孩”。

151
00:06:07.590 --> 00:06:10.750
Mindy told me that Amy was her favorite from the very beginning.
明迪告诉我，艾米从一开始就是她最喜欢的人。

152
00:06:10.750 --> 00:06:14.370
This is who she wanted to cast as the purse girl from her audition.
这就是她从试镜中选定来演“卖包女孩”的人选。

153
00:06:14.570 --> 00:06:19.350
But something that I think people don't realize is that Amy Adams wasn't Amy Adams when she
但我认为人们没有意识到的一点是，艾米·亚当斯在被选为

154
00:06:19.350 --> 00:06:20.510
was cast as the purse girl.
“卖包女孩”时，还不是后来那个艾米·亚当斯。

155
00:06:20.690 --> 00:06:22.990
She became Amy Adams later.
她是后来才成为艾米·亚当斯的。

156
00:06:23.590 --> 00:06:25.770
And that's an interesting story, actually, because we...
说起来这其实是个有趣的故事，因为我们……

157
00:06:25.770 --> 00:06:31.450
We filmed this episode in the fall of 2004, but they didn't start airing until the spring
我们是在2004年秋天拍摄这一集的，但直到2005年春天

158
00:06:31.450 --> 00:06:32.490
of 2005.
才开始播出。

159
00:06:33.190 --> 00:06:37.970
And that fall, she was nominated for an Academy Award for her role in Junebug.
而那个秋天，她就凭借在《甲壳虫》中的角色获得了奥斯卡提名。

160
00:06:38.130 --> 00:06:38.290
Right.
没错。

161
00:06:38.410 --> 00:06:41.950
When she did this episode of The Office, no one had seen Junebug yet, because Junebug
当她拍摄《办公室》这一集时，还没人看过《甲壳虫》，因为《甲壳虫》

162
00:06:41.950 --> 00:06:43.970
came out in August of 2005.
是在2005年8月才上映的。

163
00:06:44.210 --> 00:06:44.370
Yes.
是的。

164
00:06:44.550 --> 00:06:48.670
And I remember her first day on set, we were talking, and I was like, how are things
我记得她第一天到片场时，我们聊天，我问她，最近怎么样？

165
00:06:48.670 --> 00:06:48.950
going?
她说，嗯，你知道，还行吧。

166
00:06:49.050 --> 00:06:50.210
She's like, well, you know, it's good.
我是说，我之前在CBS的一部叫《拉斯维加斯医生》的剧里演过，但他们把我解雇了。

167
00:06:50.210 --> 00:06:55.070
I mean, I was on a show on CBS called Dr. Vegas, but they let me go.
哦，对，没错。

168
00:06:55.570 --> 00:06:56.450
Oh, that's right.
她说，我算是被炒鱿鱼了。

169
00:06:56.690 --> 00:06:58.070
She was like, I kind of got fired.
我说，不会吧。

170
00:06:58.130 --> 00:06:58.830
And I was like, no.
她说，真的。

171
00:06:59.030 --> 00:06:59.590
And she was like, yeah.
我当时真的很沮丧。

172
00:06:59.670 --> 00:07:00.650
And I was really down.
我感到很失落。

173
00:07:00.910 --> 00:07:01.890
And I was bummed out.
但后来，你知道，我拍了一部叫《甲壳虫》的小成本独立电影。

174
00:07:02.050 --> 00:07:05.050
But then, you know, I did this little indie movie called Junebug.
我对它感觉很好。

175
00:07:05.230 --> 00:07:07.070
And I feel so good about it.
它会在今年晚些时候上映。

176
00:07:07.110 --> 00:07:08.550
And it's going to come out later in the year.
我说，哦，那听起来太棒了。

177
00:07:08.650 --> 00:07:10.030
And I was like, oh, that sounds great.
没错。

178
00:07:10.410 --> 00:07:10.630
Yeah.
让我来鼓励你一下，艾米·亚当斯。

179
00:07:10.630 --> 00:07:12.330
Let me build you up, Amy AdaMs.
艾米，你会没事的。

180
00:07:12.710 --> 00:07:14.470
Amy, you're going to be just fine.
而她确实没事。

181
00:07:15.470 --> 00:07:16.370
And she was.
她确实没事。

182
00:07:16.430 --> 00:07:16.930
And she was.
但艾米真的是最善良的人之一。

183
00:07:16.970 --> 00:07:19.350
But Amy is one of the nicest people.
她真的非常、非常甜美。

184
00:07:19.770 --> 00:07:21.430
She's so, so sweet.
哦，我太喜欢艾米了。

185
00:07:21.690 --> 00:07:22.910
Oh, I loved Amy.
和她一起工作真是太有趣了。

186
00:07:23.090 --> 00:07:25.070
It was so fun working with her.
拍摄结束后，有很多粉丝问我们是否计划让这个角色回归。

187
00:07:25.470 --> 00:07:30.510
There were a lot of questions from fans asking if we planned to bring this character back
嗯，我们当时都没想过我们的剧能续订下去。

188
00:07:30.510 --> 00:07:31.530
after we shot it.
没错。

189
00:07:31.710 --> 00:07:33.470
Well, we didn't think we were going to have a show.
当时确实没有让她回归的计划。

190
00:07:33.670 --> 00:07:33.950
Right.
但后来剧集续订了，他们就想让她回来。

191
00:07:34.130 --> 00:07:36.010
There were no real plans to bring her back.
但现在她已经是获得奥斯卡提名的艾米·亚当斯了。

192
00:07:36.130 --> 00:07:39.390
But then when the show got picked up, they wanted to bring her back.
我当时想，好吧，希望我们能请她回来。

193
00:07:39.390 --> 00:07:42.470
But now she was Academy Award nominated Amy AdaMs.
我们确实做到了。

194
00:07:44.370 --> 00:07:46.130
I was like, well, I hope we can get her back.
她又回来拍了两集。

195
00:07:46.190 --> 00:07:46.670
And we did.
是的。

196
00:07:46.790 --> 00:07:48.110
She came back for two more episodes.
而且她还是帕姆和吉姆他们之间非常棒的衬托角色。

197
00:07:48.390 --> 00:07:48.690
Yes.
我喜欢看那段剧情的发展。

198
00:07:48.890 --> 00:07:53.110
And she was such a great foil, too, for Pam and Jim and all of that.
艾米·亚当斯不仅在片场超级友善，而且和她共事简直是一种享受。

199
00:07:53.210 --> 00:07:54.530
I loved watching that play out.
她真的是个很棒的人。

200
00:07:54.690 --> 00:07:58.990
Not only was Amy Adams super nice on set and just like such a pleasure to work with.
我真的非常喜欢她。

201
00:07:59.110 --> 00:08:02.710
But I don't know, probably like two years later, I ran into her.
但我不知道，大概两年后吧，我偶遇了她。

202
00:08:02.890 --> 00:08:04.730
I had a friend visiting from Alabama.
当时有个阿拉巴马州的朋友来找我。

203
00:08:05.330 --> 00:08:07.550
And you guys, I don't ever go out.
你们知道的，我平时从不出门。

204
00:08:07.550 --> 00:08:08.910
So my friend was coming in town.
所以朋友要来城里了。

205
00:08:09.050 --> 00:08:11.110
And I was like, oh, I'm going to take her somewhere fancy.
我就想，噢，我要带她去个高档的地方。

206
00:08:11.950 --> 00:08:13.970
That hotel, Chateau Marmont, that's fancy.
那家酒店，马尔蒙庄园酒店，那地方很高级。

207
00:08:14.090 --> 00:08:14.690
We'll go there.
我们就去那儿吧。

208
00:08:14.790 --> 00:08:15.790
Because I just had it in my head.
因为我脑子里一直这么想。

209
00:08:15.890 --> 00:08:17.450
Yeah, like the Hollywood fancy place to eat.
对，就像是好莱坞那种高级餐厅。

210
00:08:17.450 --> 00:08:18.110
It was a fancy place.
那确实是个高档地方。

211
00:08:18.210 --> 00:08:18.370
Yeah.
是啊。

212
00:08:18.530 --> 00:08:19.990
I mean, it's like half an hour from my house.
我是说，离我家大概半小时车程。

213
00:08:20.050 --> 00:08:21.170
It was such a hall.
那真是太远了。

214
00:08:21.330 --> 00:08:23.370
But I was like, no, I'll take my friend from Alabama there.
但我还是想，不，我得带我那位阿拉巴马的朋友去那儿。

215
00:08:23.570 --> 00:08:24.350
So we went.
于是我们就去了。

216
00:08:24.470 --> 00:08:26.010
And we were having dinner.
我们正在吃晚餐。

217
00:08:26.570 --> 00:08:28.190
And Amy Adams was at a table.
艾米·亚当斯也在那儿用餐。

218
00:08:28.590 --> 00:08:32.110
And she sent over two glasses of champagne to my friend and I.
她给我们俩送了两杯香槟过来。

219
00:08:32.430 --> 00:08:34.450
And I was like, they were like, oh, this is so classy.
我当时就觉得，她们说，噢，这太有格调了。

220
00:08:34.450 --> 00:08:35.670
Classy move, Amy AdaMs.
真有格调，艾米·亚当斯。

221
00:08:35.670 --> 00:08:37.250
And I was like, who's this from?
我当时问，这是谁送的？

222
00:08:37.390 --> 00:08:38.950
They were like, it's from Amy AdaMs.
她们说是艾米·亚当斯送的。

223
00:08:39.230 --> 00:08:40.110
And she waved.
然后她还向我们挥了挥手。

224
00:08:40.190 --> 00:08:41.390
And then she came over and we chatted.
接着她走过来，我们聊了几句。

225
00:08:41.610 --> 00:08:43.170
Amy Adams is just a class act.
艾米·亚当斯真是个有风度的人。

226
00:08:43.310 --> 00:08:47.510
I have a funny Amy Adams story about how people think that we look alike.
关于人们觉得我和她长得像，我还有一个关于艾米·亚当斯的趣事。

227
00:08:48.050 --> 00:08:51.190
So she and I were both at this work party thing.
当时我和她都在参加一个工作派对之类的活动。

228
00:08:51.250 --> 00:08:52.450
I can't remember exactly.
具体我也记不清了。

229
00:08:52.630 --> 00:08:55.470
I think it was like honoring directors in the industry.
我想大概是向业内导演致敬的活动吧。

230
00:08:55.470 --> 00:08:56.570
And we were both there.
我们都在场。

231
00:08:56.670 --> 00:08:58.290
And my friend came up to me.
然后我有个朋友走过来。

232
00:08:58.350 --> 00:09:01.030
And he said, I am so humiliated right now.
他说，我现在真是尴尬透了。

233
00:09:01.330 --> 00:09:02.590
And I said, what happened?
我问，发生什么事了？

234
00:09:02.590 --> 00:09:09.110
And he goes, I just went up and bear hugged Amy Adams and said, Jenna, you look beautiful.
他说，我刚才走过去给了艾米·亚当斯一个熊抱，还说，珍娜，你看起来真美。

235
00:09:09.270 --> 00:09:09.910
Oh, no.
噢，不。

236
00:09:10.150 --> 00:09:11.270
Because he mixed us up.
因为他把我们认错了。

237
00:09:11.390 --> 00:09:14.410
And people have this thing where they think she and I look a lot alike.
人们总觉得我和她长得很像。

238
00:09:14.630 --> 00:09:17.130
We really don't look anything alike in person.
其实我们本人长得一点都不像。

239
00:09:17.130 --> 00:09:20.410
Although I guess I just told a story about someone who mixed us up in person.
虽然我刚才好像刚讲了一个人把我们本人认错的故事。

240
00:09:20.650 --> 00:09:21.970
I mean, there is a resemblance.
我是说，确实有那么点相似之处。

241
00:09:22.290 --> 00:09:25.430
She's perfectly cast because there is a resemblance.
她选角选得很准，因为确实有相似之处。

242
00:09:25.430 --> 00:09:27.050
And you're both like beautiful ladies.
而且你们都是大美女。

243
00:09:27.490 --> 00:09:27.750
Thanks.
谢谢。

244
00:09:27.910 --> 00:09:29.770
But I see a resemblance.
但我确实能看出相似的地方。

245
00:09:29.910 --> 00:09:31.070
I feel like we could play sisters.
我觉得我们可以演姐妹。

246
00:09:31.450 --> 00:09:31.970
You could.
你们确实可以。

247
00:09:32.270 --> 00:09:33.010
All right, Hollywood.
好了，好莱坞。

248
00:09:33.230 --> 00:09:34.230
You heard it here firSt.
你们在这里先听到了。

249
00:09:34.450 --> 00:09:36.930
That's how I, that's, I guess that's how I talk when I'm talking to Hollywood.
这就是我，我想，这就是我跟好莱坞说话的方式。

250
00:09:37.130 --> 00:09:37.890
I guess it is.
我想确实是这样。

251
00:09:38.070 --> 00:09:39.190
Hollywood beware.
好莱坞，小心了。

252
00:09:39.670 --> 00:09:40.030
Hollywood.
好莱坞。

253
00:09:40.330 --> 00:09:42.030
This is Angela Kinsey.
我是安吉拉·金赛。

254
00:09:42.290 --> 00:09:43.070
I don't love it.
我不喜欢这个。

255
00:09:44.710 --> 00:09:48.940
I think your character, your Hollywood voice lady.
我觉得你的角色，你那个好莱坞嗓音的女士。

256
00:09:49.000 --> 00:09:49.880
I think you should work on it.
我觉得你应该再练练。

257
00:09:49.940 --> 00:09:50.320
Okay, thanks.
好的，谢谢。

258
00:09:50.320 --> 00:09:51.040
Give it an accent.
加点口音。

259
00:09:51.260 --> 00:09:51.360
Oh.
哦。

260
00:09:51.520 --> 00:09:52.300
Should it be British?
是要英式口音吗？

261
00:09:52.660 --> 00:09:53.580
I, Hollywood.
我，好莱坞。

262
00:09:54.080 --> 00:09:54.220
No.
不是。

263
00:09:54.400 --> 00:09:54.820
Oh, my God.
天哪。

264
00:09:54.820 --> 00:09:56.860
Oh, that's Australian.
哦，那是澳大利亚口音。

265
00:09:57.340 --> 00:09:58.620
Oh, what was that?
哦，刚才那是啥？

266
00:09:58.880 --> 00:10:00.580
That was like drunk Scottish.
听起来像喝醉的苏格兰人。

267
00:10:00.600 --> 00:10:01.640
What is happening?
到底怎么回事？

268
00:10:01.920 --> 00:10:03.000
I can't do accents.
我不会模仿口音。

269
00:10:03.000 --> 00:10:04.280
And I also can't sing.
而且我也不会唱歌。

270
00:10:04.520 --> 00:10:07.540
I can do Australian, but I grew up overseas and all my best friends were Aussies.
我会说澳大利亚口音，因为我是在海外长大的，我最好的朋友都是澳大利亚人。

271
00:10:07.860 --> 00:10:10.260
So right now, I'm just sitting here talking to Jenna.
所以现在，我只是坐在这里和珍娜聊天。

272
00:10:10.540 --> 00:10:12.060
We're going to talk about Hot Girl.
我们要聊聊《辣妹》那一集。

273
00:10:12.260 --> 00:10:12.540
Yeah.
没错。

274
00:10:12.760 --> 00:10:13.880
That's really good, Ange.
那真的很棒，安吉。

275
00:10:13.920 --> 00:10:14.440
Oh, thanks.
哦，谢谢。

276
00:10:14.560 --> 00:10:15.540
Thanks so much.
太感谢了。

277
00:10:16.480 --> 00:10:17.240
I'm shocked.
我很震惊。

278
00:10:17.580 --> 00:10:18.860
I'm genuinely impressed.
我真心感到佩服。

279
00:10:19.180 --> 00:10:20.000
Okay, okay, okay.
好吧，好吧，好吧。

280
00:10:20.020 --> 00:10:23.020
See, that was so good, but your Hollywood voice is a no.
你看，刚才那个很好，但你的好莱坞嗓音真的不行。

281
00:10:23.200 --> 00:10:23.500
I know.
我知道。

282
00:10:23.620 --> 00:10:24.060
You know what?
你知道吗？

283
00:10:24.060 --> 00:10:25.640
It's whenever I'm trying to be slick.
每当我试图表现得圆滑时就会这样。

284
00:10:26.360 --> 00:10:28.900
I am just not programmed to be slick.
我的设定里就没有圆滑这一项。

285
00:10:29.180 --> 00:10:30.600
This is true about you.
这一点你说得对。

286
00:10:30.720 --> 00:10:31.180
I know.
我知道。

287
00:10:31.440 --> 00:10:36.440
Before we go to a break, since we're talking about Amy Adams and how wonderful she is both
在进入休息之前，既然我们提到了艾米·亚当斯，以及她在片场内外有多么出色，

288
00:10:36.440 --> 00:10:41.160
on and off set, we have to tell the story about how she helped us meet Meryl Streep.
我们必须讲讲她是如何帮我们见到梅丽尔·斯特里普的故事。

289
00:10:41.400 --> 00:10:42.380
Oh, my God.
天哪。

290
00:10:42.580 --> 00:10:43.220
Oh, my God.
天哪。

291
00:10:43.360 --> 00:10:45.360
I cannot believe I didn't put that on a note card.
真不敢相信我没把这事写在提示卡上。

292
00:10:45.400 --> 00:10:46.300
I can't believe it either.
我也真不敢相信。

293
00:10:46.300 --> 00:10:47.100
What is wrong with me?
我这是怎么了？

294
00:10:47.180 --> 00:10:47.340
You know what?
你知道吗？

295
00:10:47.340 --> 00:10:47.860
I don't know.
我不知道。

296
00:10:47.980 --> 00:10:48.500
I got here.
我刚到这儿。

297
00:10:48.580 --> 00:10:49.120
There were donuts.
有甜甜圈。

298
00:10:49.280 --> 00:10:49.920
I got excited.
我太兴奋了。

299
00:10:49.920 --> 00:10:50.480
I forgot.
我就给忘了。

300
00:10:50.800 --> 00:10:51.040
Okay.
好吧。

301
00:10:54.060 --> 00:10:54.920
The Golden Globes.
金球奖。

302
00:10:55.080 --> 00:10:55.320
Oh.
噢。

303
00:10:55.680 --> 00:10:57.500
The office had been nominated.
办公室剧组获得了提名。

304
00:10:57.520 --> 00:11:04.300
And I have to say, first of all, Angela, I am so grateful that I got to go to these award
首先我得说，安吉拉，我非常感激能和你一起去参加这些颁奖

305
00:11:04.300 --> 00:11:05.400
show things with you.
典礼。

306
00:11:05.600 --> 00:11:06.240
I know.
我知道。

307
00:11:06.340 --> 00:11:07.160
Well, here's the thing.
是这样的。

308
00:11:07.280 --> 00:11:08.960
We didn't go to fancy parties.
我们没去参加什么高档派对。

309
00:11:08.960 --> 00:11:10.200
You guys, we're not fancy people.
伙计们，我们可不是什么时髦的人。

310
00:11:10.360 --> 00:11:12.160
I'm intimate dinner party person.
我更适合那种私密的晚餐聚会。

311
00:11:12.380 --> 00:11:13.220
Well, I...
嗯，我……

312
00:11:13.220 --> 00:11:14.140
It was like a small group.
就像是一个小团体。

313
00:11:14.360 --> 00:11:18.820
I think the fanciest parties I'd ever been to were just like when one of my friends would
我想我参加过最豪华的派对，大概也就是朋友举办的

314
00:11:18.820 --> 00:11:19.540
have a big wedding.
盛大婚礼了。

315
00:11:19.800 --> 00:11:24.440
But I am so glad that I got to navigate all that stuff with you because I would normally
但我很高兴能和你一起应对这一切，因为通常在这种场合

316
00:11:24.440 --> 00:11:26.520
kind of freeze up at something like that.
