00:17:15.910 --> 00:17:20.050
And the top seller in the office is going to get a prize worth $1,000.
办公室里业绩最好的销售将获得价值1000美元的奖品。

479
00:17:20.570 --> 00:17:23.410
And that Michael can choose what that prize is.
而且迈克尔可以决定奖品是什么。

480
00:17:23.790 --> 00:17:24.230
The end.
结束。

481
00:17:26.030 --> 00:17:29.850
So I love that this episode starts with the line,
我很喜欢这一集开头的这句台词，

482
00:17:29.990 --> 00:17:31.590
are you listening to me, Michael?
你在听我说话吗，迈克尔？

483
00:17:32.470 --> 00:17:33.370
By Jan.
简说的。

484
00:17:33.690 --> 00:17:35.870
Because he's just like futzing around with pencils.
因为他当时就在那儿摆弄铅笔。

485
00:17:35.950 --> 00:17:37.170
And he has her own speakerphone.
而且他开了免提。

486
00:17:37.350 --> 00:17:41.070
But I love that the first scene, you just think he's being an idiot.
但我喜欢第一个场景，你以为他只是在犯蠢。

487
00:17:41.070 --> 00:17:43.630
And then you hear this voice say, are you listening to me, Michael?
然后你听到这个声音说，你在听我说话吗，迈克尔？

488
00:17:43.970 --> 00:17:45.810
And I just love it.
我太喜欢这个了。

489
00:17:45.950 --> 00:17:46.490
I love it.
我太喜欢了。

490
00:17:47.250 --> 00:17:51.410
The next scene when Dwight is standing over Michael's shoulder in the talking head,
下一个场景是德怀特站在迈克尔身后进行访谈时，

491
00:17:51.470 --> 00:17:52.810
it begins as a talking head.
一开始是访谈形式。

492
00:17:52.910 --> 00:17:56.450
And then it reveals that Dwight is kind of like hovering.
然后揭示出德怀特其实一直像幽灵一样徘徊在后面。

493
00:17:56.730 --> 00:17:58.090
That's the first time we did that.
那是我们第一次那样做。

494
00:17:58.270 --> 00:18:00.910
But then we will do that many times in the show.
但后来我们在剧中多次使用了这种手法。

495
00:18:01.050 --> 00:18:05.230
It's one of my favorite things is how Dwight stands over Michael's shoulder.
德怀特站在迈克尔身后这种设定是我最喜欢的部分之一。

496
00:18:05.710 --> 00:18:09.910
That's also when Pam comes into the office to say someone wants to sell handbags.
那也是帕姆走进办公室说有人想卖手提包的时候。

497
00:18:09.950 --> 00:18:13.670
And Michael is totally against it, of course, until he sees how attractive the woman is.
迈克尔当然是完全反对的，直到他看到那个女人有多迷人。

498
00:18:14.170 --> 00:18:18.030
A lot of people wrote in and wanted to know,
很多人写信来问，

499
00:18:18.210 --> 00:18:20.610
where did these purses come from that she's selling?
她卖的这些包是从哪儿来的？

500
00:18:20.810 --> 00:18:22.110
So I called Phil Shea.
所以我打电话问了菲尔·谢。

501
00:18:22.250 --> 00:18:23.050
Our prop master.
我们的道具师。

502
00:18:23.190 --> 00:18:23.490
Yes.
是的。

503
00:18:23.790 --> 00:18:26.730
He told me that he bought them all in downtown LA.
他告诉我这些都是他在洛杉矶市中心买的。

504
00:18:26.990 --> 00:18:28.310
Oh, at like the markets downtown?
哦，是在市中心的那些市场吗？

505
00:18:28.610 --> 00:18:28.910
Yes.
是的。

506
00:18:28.910 --> 00:18:30.770
Oh, the knockoff purse market?
哦，是卖仿冒包的市场吗？

507
00:18:30.910 --> 00:18:31.150
Yes.
是的。

508
00:18:31.470 --> 00:18:35.230
Because some of them looked really nice, but also they looked a little like pleather.
因为有些看起来确实不错，但看起来也有点像人造革。

509
00:18:35.410 --> 00:18:36.710
I don't think anyone kept them.
我觉得没人留着它们。

510
00:18:36.830 --> 00:18:37.510
I didn't keep one.
我没留。

511
00:18:37.510 --> 00:18:37.830
Did you?
你留了吗？

512
00:18:38.010 --> 00:18:38.810
I didn't know we could.
我不知道我们可以留。

513
00:18:38.810 --> 00:18:40.190
I probably would have taken one.
我当时可能会拿一个。

514
00:18:40.330 --> 00:18:44.330
It was early on when we weren't brave enough to ask to take things yet.
那是早期，我们还没胆量开口要东西。

515
00:18:44.410 --> 00:18:44.950
Yeah, no.
是啊，没要。

516
00:18:45.670 --> 00:18:49.770
Later when the show wrapped, I did take Pam's everyday purse.
后来剧集杀青时，我确实拿走了帕姆的日常用包。

517
00:18:50.310 --> 00:18:54.250
It's just something that had been sitting, even if I didn't use it in a scene,
那东西一直放在那儿，就算我没在戏里用过，

518
00:18:54.390 --> 00:18:56.730
it sat on Pam's desk or it was in her drawer.
它也一直放在帕姆的桌子上或者抽屉里。

519
00:18:57.070 --> 00:18:57.330
Yeah.
是啊。

520
00:18:57.490 --> 00:18:58.390
So I have that.
所以我留着那个。

521
00:18:58.390 --> 00:19:02.630
I have Pam's everyday purse that she had for most of the season.
我有帕姆大部分时间都在用的那个日常包。

522
00:19:02.930 --> 00:19:04.630
But I didn't keep a fancy purse.
但我没留那个时髦的包。

523
00:19:04.870 --> 00:19:10.750
There's the scene where Michael has to refer to Katie, the purse girl, as Pam 6.0.
有一场戏是迈克尔必须把凯蒂，那个卖包的女孩，称为帕姆6.0版本。

524
00:19:11.690 --> 00:19:13.710
This was not an improvisation.
这不是即兴发挥。

525
00:19:14.330 --> 00:19:15.970
I have the script.
我有剧本。

526
00:19:16.110 --> 00:19:16.490
I know.
我知道。

527
00:19:16.610 --> 00:19:16.790
I know.
我知道。

528
00:19:16.990 --> 00:19:17.390
From Hot Girl.
出自《辣妹》那一集。

529
00:19:17.610 --> 00:19:19.450
I have all the scripts from season one.
我有第一季所有的剧本。

530
00:19:19.450 --> 00:19:21.470
I saved them, speaking of saving things.
我把它们留下了，说到留下东西。

531
00:19:21.590 --> 00:19:22.830
And I looked it up.
我查了一下。

532
00:19:23.010 --> 00:19:25.230
She is like the improved version of me.
她就像是我的升级版。

533
00:19:25.370 --> 00:19:26.570
She is not.
她才不是。

534
00:19:26.790 --> 00:19:27.790
Yes, she is.
不，她是。

535
00:19:27.790 --> 00:19:28.130
She is not.
她不是。

536
00:19:28.230 --> 00:19:28.870
She is.
她是。

537
00:19:28.950 --> 00:19:30.990
As your best friend, I am not going to let that slide.
作为你最好的朋友，我可不能让你这么说。

538
00:19:31.170 --> 00:19:31.750
She is not.
她不是。

539
00:19:32.010 --> 00:19:34.950
But in this episode, they had really zhuzhed her up.
但在这一集里，他们确实把她打扮得很亮眼。

540
00:19:35.110 --> 00:19:36.810
She had a push-up bra on and her hair off.
她穿了聚拢文胸，头发也弄上去了。

541
00:19:36.810 --> 00:19:37.390
It doesn't matter.
那不重要。

542
00:19:37.670 --> 00:19:42.110
Even on our plainest day, Amy Adams is Jenna 6.0.
就算在我们最朴素的时候，艾米·亚当斯也是珍娜的6.0版本。

543
00:19:42.230 --> 00:19:42.630
She is.
她是。

544
00:19:42.690 --> 00:19:43.210
No, she's not.
不，她不是。

545
00:19:43.210 --> 00:19:44.130
It's okay with me.
我没关系。

546
00:19:44.130 --> 00:19:44.810
No, I'm not.
不，我不是。

547
00:19:45.310 --> 00:19:45.550
No.
不。

548
00:19:45.730 --> 00:19:46.590
Well, oh, okay.
好吧，哦，好吧。

549
00:19:46.930 --> 00:19:47.610
Well, whatever.
好吧，随它去吧。

550
00:19:47.850 --> 00:19:49.050
Should I have not said that?
我是不是不该那么说？

551
00:19:49.350 --> 00:19:51.710
No, I think you, no, I think it's a funny story.
不，我觉得你……不，我觉得这是一个有趣的故事。

552
00:19:51.810 --> 00:19:55.810
But as your best friend, I'm not going to let you say Amy Adams is a better version of you.
但作为你最好的朋友，我绝不会让你说艾米·亚当斯是你的升级版。

553
00:19:55.950 --> 00:19:58.970
It's like we look similar, but then her nose is a little daintier.
就像我们看起来很像，但她的鼻子更精致一点。

554
00:19:59.370 --> 00:20:03.730
And her cheeks are a little rosier and her hair is just a little brighter red.
她的脸颊更红润一点，头发的红色也更鲜亮一点。

555
00:20:04.010 --> 00:20:04.770
You know what I'm saying?
你明白我的意思吗？

556
00:20:04.770 --> 00:20:08.630
It's just like she just turned it up a couple of notches on the dial and you get Amy AdaMs.
就像是把刻度盘调高了几档，然后你就成了艾米·亚当斯。

557
00:20:08.770 --> 00:20:11.390
Like if you're creating me, right, you get to me.
比如如果你在创造我，对吧，你得到了现在的我。

558
00:20:11.530 --> 00:20:14.810
And then if you turn the dial a couple more notches, it turns into Amy AdaMs.
然后如果你再把刻度盘调高几档，就变成了艾米·亚当斯。

559
00:20:15.770 --> 00:20:16.730
She's Disney you.
她是迪士尼版的你。

560
00:20:17.030 --> 00:20:17.810
She kind of is.
某种程度上确实是。

561
00:20:17.850 --> 00:20:19.410
She's the Disney princess version of me.
她是迪士尼公主版的我。

562
00:20:19.590 --> 00:20:19.890
Yes.
没错。

563
00:20:20.110 --> 00:20:21.170
Angela, do you have a note card?
安吉拉，你手里有笔记卡吗？

564
00:20:21.290 --> 00:20:23.030
Because you're like handling a note card right now.
因为你现在好像在摆弄一张笔记卡。

565
00:20:23.090 --> 00:20:24.510
I feel like you want to say a note card.
我觉得你想说点笔记卡上的内容。

566
00:20:24.510 --> 00:20:27.170
I mean, it's in your hand and then you're touching them.
我是说，它在你手里，你一直在摸它。

567
00:20:27.390 --> 00:20:28.350
What is it that you want to say?
你到底想说什么？

568
00:20:28.850 --> 00:20:30.430
Are you annoyed that I'm touching?
你是因为我在摸它而感到烦躁吗？

569
00:20:30.490 --> 00:20:33.490
No, I'm giving you and I'm giving you a chance to speak.
不，我是在给你，给你一个说话的机会。

570
00:20:36.230 --> 00:20:38.810
Oh, thank you so much.
哦，太感谢你了。

571
00:20:40.490 --> 00:20:43.530
Oh, so it's British when you are offended.
哦，所以你被冒犯的时候就会说英式英语。

572
00:20:43.870 --> 00:20:44.210
Oh, God.
天哪。

573
00:20:44.410 --> 00:20:45.110
No, stop.
不，停下。

574
00:20:45.350 --> 00:20:45.570
Stop.
停下。

575
00:20:46.110 --> 00:20:50.790
I was just going to say that Michael Scott has a talking head that I love so much.
我只是想说，迈克尔·斯科特有一个我非常喜欢的采访镜头。

576
00:20:50.910 --> 00:20:54.190
And these are just one of these talking heads that they're in every episode.
这些采访镜头是每一集里都会有的那种。

577
00:20:54.190 --> 00:20:57.930
And getting to rewatch them, I'm like, ah, my God, that's brilliant.
重温的时候，我心想，天哪，这太精彩了。

578
00:20:58.270 --> 00:20:59.370
Is it the small businessman?
是关于那个小企业主吗？

579
00:20:59.690 --> 00:21:00.290
I love it.
我喜欢那个。

580
00:21:00.430 --> 00:21:01.270
Is it the things that he reads?
是他读的那些东西吗？

581
00:21:01.470 --> 00:21:05.510
I love that he said he loves American Way magazine, the in-flight magazine.
我特别喜欢他说他喜欢《美国之路》杂志，就是那种机上杂志。

582
00:21:05.730 --> 00:21:10.430
And then he goes, they did a great profile on Doris Roberts and where she likes to eat
然后他说，他们对多丽丝·罗伯茨做了一篇很棒的专访，介绍了她喜欢去哪里吃饭，

583
00:21:10.430 --> 00:21:11.490
when she's in Phoenix.
当她在菲尼克斯的时候。

584
00:21:11.810 --> 00:21:14.530
It just made me laugh so hard because I read those.
这让我笑得不行，因为我也看那些杂志。

585
00:21:14.690 --> 00:21:19.070
I just want you to know American Airlines, whenever I fly with you, I get the American
我只想让美国航空知道，每次我坐你们的飞机，我都会拿出《美国之路》杂志，

586
00:21:19.070 --> 00:21:21.410
way out and I look to see where people eat.
看看名人们都在哪儿吃饭。

587
00:21:21.750 --> 00:21:23.110
It made me laugh so hard.
这真的让我笑得不行。

588
00:21:23.110 --> 00:21:24.890
And then he's like, illuminating.
然后他说，真有启发性。

589
00:21:25.230 --> 00:21:26.950
I love those magazines, too.
我也喜欢那些杂志。

590
00:21:27.150 --> 00:21:28.070
I read them.
我也会读。

591
00:21:28.350 --> 00:21:31.890
And, you know, actually, one of the coolest things that ever happened to me is that one
而且，你知道吗，其实我经历过最酷的事情之一就是有一次，

592
00:21:31.890 --> 00:21:34.530
time I had an article in...
我有一篇文章登在……

593
00:21:34.530 --> 00:21:35.610
In an in-flight magazine?
登在机上杂志里？

594
00:21:35.630 --> 00:21:36.030
Yes.
是的。

595
00:21:36.130 --> 00:21:38.190
Just like the Doris Roberts thing, I got profiled.
就像多丽丝·罗伯茨那样，我被采访了。

596
00:21:38.450 --> 00:21:38.790
What?
什么？

597
00:21:38.970 --> 00:21:39.190
Yeah.
是啊。

598
00:21:39.350 --> 00:21:40.490
I would be so excited.
我会兴奋死的。

599
00:21:40.650 --> 00:21:41.390
Why didn't you tell me?
你为什么没告诉我？

600
00:21:41.510 --> 00:21:42.190
That is so cool.
那太酷了。

601
00:21:42.350 --> 00:21:45.890
No, I told this story about playing poker in Scotland.
不，我讲过那个在苏格兰打扑克的故事。

602
00:21:46.330 --> 00:21:47.410
Oh, wait, wait.
噢，等等，等等。

603
00:21:47.450 --> 00:21:48.950
I know this is a total tangent.
我知道这完全扯远了。

604
00:21:49.390 --> 00:21:50.010
Guys, I'm sorry.
伙计们，抱歉。

605
00:21:50.010 --> 00:21:52.370
I have to take Jen on a tangent because I love this story.
我得带珍扯远一点，因为我太喜欢这个故事了。

606
00:21:52.670 --> 00:21:53.430
Yeah, should I tell this story?
是啊，我要讲这个故事吗？

607
00:21:53.510 --> 00:21:54.510
You have to tell it.
你一定要讲。

608
00:21:54.630 --> 00:21:54.770
Okay.
好吧。

609
00:21:54.770 --> 00:21:57.270
Because, first of all, it makes you sound way cooler than you are.
因为首先，这让你听起来比实际酷多了。

610
00:21:57.330 --> 00:21:57.750
No offense.
没有冒犯的意思。

611
00:21:58.070 --> 00:21:58.310
I know.
我知道。

612
00:21:58.310 --> 00:21:59.970
But it kind of makes you sound like a rock star.
但这让你听起来有点像摇滚明星。

613
00:22:00.090 --> 00:22:02.210
It's my biggest rock star moment of my life.
这是我人生中最摇滚的时刻。

614
00:22:02.530 --> 00:22:03.050
It's pretty...
这相当……

615
00:22:03.050 --> 00:22:03.750
A hundred percent.
百分之百。

616
00:22:03.770 --> 00:22:04.090
Okay.
好吧。

617
00:22:04.270 --> 00:22:05.570
So, I had no...
所以，我当时没……

618
00:22:05.570 --> 00:22:09.310
I know you're going to tell that story, but I need to see that in-flight magazine article.
我知道你要讲那个故事，但我得先看看那篇机上杂志的文章。

619
00:22:09.330 --> 00:22:09.790
I'll show it to you.
我会给你看的。

620
00:22:09.850 --> 00:22:11.970
It was for United magazine.
那是为美联航杂志写的。

621
00:22:12.670 --> 00:22:18.130
And they had this story where they wanted people to tell the craziest ways they've ever
他们当时有个专题，想让人们分享自己克服时差最疯狂的方法。

622
00:22:18.130 --> 00:22:19.170
fought jet lag.
克服时差。

623
00:22:20.030 --> 00:22:24.030
So, Lee and I had this little romantic trip that we took to Scotland.
当时我和李去苏格兰进行了一次小小的浪漫旅行。

624
00:22:24.030 --> 00:22:25.530
This was before we had children.
那是在我们有孩子之前。

625
00:22:25.810 --> 00:22:29.330
I remember this because you told me you were going and I was like, well, that's not a lot
我记得这件事，因为你告诉我你要去的时候，我说，嗯，那没几天啊。

626
00:22:29.330 --> 00:22:30.170
of days.
几天。

627
00:22:30.470 --> 00:22:34.050
Yeah, we only had five days because we had a one-week hiatus from work.
是啊，我们只有五天时间，因为我们工作有一周的假期。

628
00:22:34.190 --> 00:22:35.830
This is what people without children can do.
这就是没孩子的人能做的事。

629
00:22:35.830 --> 00:22:39.970
Yeah, we can just jet off to Scotland for five days.
是啊，我们可以直接飞去苏格兰玩五天。

630
00:22:40.210 --> 00:22:42.970
So, we were going to spend two days in Edinburgh.
所以，我们打算在爱丁堡待两天。

631
00:22:43.270 --> 00:22:43.470
Okay.
好的。

632
00:22:43.530 --> 00:22:48.210
And then we were going to go into the countryside for the other three days, do a tour of a, you
然后剩下的三天去乡下，参观一下，你知道，比如威士忌酒厂之类的，所有真正有趣的事情。

633
00:22:48.210 --> 00:22:51.290
know, like a scotch factory and everything really fun.
你知道，比如威士忌酒厂之类的，所有真正有趣的事情。

634
00:22:51.570 --> 00:22:54.790
So, we get there and we thought we will take an overnight flight.
所以，我们到了那里，心想我们要坐夜班飞机。

635
00:22:54.910 --> 00:23:00.710
We will sleep on the plane and we will arrive at noon rested and ready to tour Edinburgh.
我们要在飞机上睡觉，然后中午到达，休息好，准备游览爱丁堡。

636
00:23:01.070 --> 00:23:01.730
Yeah, right.
是啊，想得美。

637
00:23:01.950 --> 00:23:02.950
This did not happen.
这根本没发生。

638
00:23:02.950 --> 00:23:04.570
We did not sleep on the plane.
我们没在飞机上睡着。

