他就在我身边徘徊，还羞辱我。

810
00:28:44.010 --> 00:28:45.130
And I could not get through it.
我根本演不下去。

811
00:28:45.290 --> 00:28:48.770
Every time he would start his sentence, it would make me laugh.
每次他一开口，我就忍不住想笑。

812
00:28:49.030 --> 00:28:53.110
That was the scene that I probably laughed the most in when I was shooting this episode.
那大概是我拍这一集时笑场最多的一场戏了。

813
00:28:53.510 --> 00:28:55.850
And this leads me into a fan question from Delaney.
这让我想到了粉丝德莱尼提出的一个问题。

814
00:28:56.150 --> 00:28:58.830
Did you guys ever get offended by the scripts personally?
你们有没有因为剧本而感到被冒犯过？

815
00:28:59.130 --> 00:29:02.350
Like in this episode, how Pam is compared to Katie the whole time?
比如在这一集中，帕姆一直被拿来和凯蒂作比较？

816
00:29:02.490 --> 00:29:03.870
Jenna, did you take that personally?
珍娜，你对此感到介意吗？

817
00:29:04.550 --> 00:29:05.430
I didn't.
我没有。

818
00:29:05.430 --> 00:29:10.350
Well, I didn't either, because I felt like a lot of our comedy was it was a little bit
嗯，我也没有，因为我觉得我们的喜剧风格有点

819
00:29:10.350 --> 00:29:11.050
of a free for all.
像是随性发挥。

820
00:29:11.170 --> 00:29:15.150
Like everyone was going to have a moment, you know, where they were sort of the butt of
每个人都会有那么一刻，你知道，成为

821
00:29:15.150 --> 00:29:15.610
the joke.
笑话的对象。

822
00:29:15.810 --> 00:29:17.050
But it was never malicious.
但那绝不是恶意的。

823
00:29:17.350 --> 00:29:19.250
It was just it served the script.
那只是为了剧本服务。

824
00:29:19.410 --> 00:29:20.230
It served the story.
为了剧情服务。

825
00:29:20.450 --> 00:29:21.350
I never took offense.
我从没觉得被冒犯过。

826
00:29:21.610 --> 00:29:28.170
Also, I feel like so much of comedy and comedians is self-deprecating in nature.
而且我觉得喜剧和喜剧演员很大程度上本质上是自嘲的。

827
00:29:28.390 --> 00:29:28.590
Yeah.
没错。

828
00:29:28.750 --> 00:29:31.990
And so we're a group of people who are pretty honest with ourselves.
所以我们这群人对自己都挺坦诚的。

829
00:29:32.230 --> 00:29:32.810
Don't you think?
你不觉得吗？

830
00:29:33.050 --> 00:29:33.130
Yeah.
没错。

831
00:29:33.290 --> 00:29:34.610
It wasn't offensive to me.
我并不觉得被冒犯了。

832
00:29:34.610 --> 00:29:40.890
It was also it was the idea that has happened to all of us where a more attractive person
而且这其实是我们每个人都经历过的情况，当一个更有魅力的人

833
00:29:40.890 --> 00:29:45.890
walks in the room and is getting all the attention and then you feel you feel jealous.
走进房间，吸引了所有人的注意，你就会感到嫉妒。

834
00:29:45.970 --> 00:29:47.950
But I enjoyed this episode.
但我很喜欢这一集。

835
00:29:48.090 --> 00:29:49.870
I loved playing with all those feelings.
我很享受演绎这些情绪的过程。

836
00:29:50.030 --> 00:29:52.570
I was going to say it was a lot of human moments for Pam.
我正想说，这对帕姆来说有很多真实的人性时刻。

837
00:29:52.710 --> 00:29:56.050
Just seeing how Jim was affected and how that affected her.
看着吉姆受到的影响，以及这如何影响了她。

838
00:29:56.330 --> 00:29:57.650
And it was fantastic.
这太棒了。

839
00:29:57.650 --> 00:29:59.190
I thought you did an excellent job.
我觉得你演得非常出色。

840
00:29:59.190 --> 00:30:00.690
I have on one of my note cards.
我的卡片上写着呢。

841
00:30:00.970 --> 00:30:02.030
Where is it, Jenna?
在哪儿呢，珍娜？

842
00:30:02.530 --> 00:30:03.450
What does it say?
上面写了什么？

843
00:30:03.950 --> 00:30:04.390
Jenna.
珍娜。

844
00:30:04.390 --> 00:30:05.270
Jenna was brilliant.
珍娜太精彩了。

845
00:30:05.590 --> 00:30:06.330
She was.
确实如此。

846
00:30:06.390 --> 00:30:07.310
Thank you, Angela.
谢谢你，安吉拉。

847
00:30:07.330 --> 00:30:08.330
You were so good.
你演得太好了。

848
00:30:08.470 --> 00:30:12.150
Oh, I don't want to like get us off your I know you have your list, lady.
哦，我不想打断你的节奏，我知道你还有清单要念，女士。

849
00:30:12.350 --> 00:30:15.550
But the moment when she's like, what are you going to do?
但是当她说“你打算怎么办？”的时候。

850
00:30:15.650 --> 00:30:17.870
And he's like, oh, I think actually I'm going to see Katie.
他说，“哦，我想我其实打算去见凯蒂。”

851
00:30:18.130 --> 00:30:23.750
The look on your face as Pam, what you did with your eyes in that moment was so amazing.
你作为帕姆时的表情，那一刻你眼神的处理真是太棒了。

852
00:30:24.070 --> 00:30:24.790
It's interesting.
挺有意思的。

853
00:30:24.790 --> 00:30:34.050
You know what I gave myself as a direction in that moment in my head was when he tells you that, do not blink your eyes.
你知道吗，那一刻我在脑子里给自己的指令是，当他那样对你说的时候，千万别眨眼。

854
00:30:34.270 --> 00:30:35.450
Just stare at him.
就那样盯着他看。

855
00:30:35.670 --> 00:30:37.030
You're not affected by that.
表现得不受影响。

856
00:30:37.130 --> 00:30:38.010
And smile.
然后微笑。

857
00:30:38.250 --> 00:30:39.970
Because that is great news.
因为那是天大的好消息。

858
00:30:39.970 --> 00:30:40.790
Oh, that's great.
噢，那太棒了。

859
00:30:41.070 --> 00:30:46.790
That was her way of trying to not show how she was feeling, but then show it shows everything.
那是她试图掩饰内心感受的方式，但结果反而把一切都暴露了。

860
00:30:47.070 --> 00:30:48.190
Yeah, it showed everything.
没错，全都暴露了。

861
00:30:48.370 --> 00:30:48.930
It was so great.
真是太精彩了。

862
00:30:49.230 --> 00:30:51.610
The scene with Katie, Michael, and Toby.
凯蒂、迈克尔和托比的那场戏。

863
00:30:52.410 --> 00:30:53.990
Oh, brutal.
噢，太残忍了。

864
00:30:54.190 --> 00:30:56.650
Oh, Jenna, I watched the deleted scenes this time.
噢，珍娜，我这次看了删减片段。

865
00:30:56.750 --> 00:30:57.170
You did?
你看了？

866
00:30:57.170 --> 00:30:59.470
Yes, so I still haven't gotten a DVD player.
是啊，我还没买DVD播放机呢。

867
00:30:59.670 --> 00:31:00.490
How'd you do it?
那你怎么看的？

868
00:31:00.570 --> 00:31:01.470
I found them online.
我在网上找到的。

869
00:31:01.750 --> 00:31:02.010
Okay.
好吧。

870
00:31:02.290 --> 00:31:04.610
I don't know if it was a legal site that I went to.
我不知道我去的那个网站合不合法。

871
00:31:05.670 --> 00:31:08.450
I clicked on so many things that took me there.
我点了很多链接才跳转过去。

872
00:31:08.470 --> 00:31:09.710
So I don't know.
所以我也不清楚。

873
00:31:09.790 --> 00:31:12.030
I probably have some inappropriate things on my computer now.
我的电脑现在可能装了一些不该有的东西。

874
00:31:12.070 --> 00:31:12.470
Oh, boy.
天哪。

875
00:31:12.610 --> 00:31:14.750
No, I'm just saying I clicked away.
不，我只是说我点了很多次。

876
00:31:14.990 --> 00:31:17.410
But anyway, I watched the deleted scenes.
总之，我看了删减片段。

877
00:31:17.590 --> 00:31:25.350
And there is a longer version of that scene where Steve, I know, is just riffing on that whole idea of sad sack Toby.
那场戏有个加长版，史蒂夫在那儿即兴发挥，一直在调侃托比那个倒霉蛋的形象。

878
00:31:25.710 --> 00:31:25.890
Yeah.
是啊。

879
00:31:25.890 --> 00:31:29.310
And it just, it is so cringy.
真的，太让人尴尬了。

880
00:31:29.470 --> 00:31:30.890
Oh, I want to go back and watch that.
噢，我想回去看看那个。

881
00:31:30.970 --> 00:31:31.810
It's really good.
真的很棒。

882
00:31:31.990 --> 00:31:38.130
So what you see in the episode is just like three seconds of that moment where he's like, oh, yeah, you're divorced, right?
正片里你看到的只有那三秒钟，他当时说，噢，对了，你离婚了是吧？

883
00:31:38.250 --> 00:31:39.050
Sleeping in your car.
睡在车里。

884
00:31:39.190 --> 00:31:41.890
I loved the, you slept one night in your car, right?
我特别喜欢那句，你还在车里睡了一晚，对吧？

885
00:31:42.050 --> 00:31:42.170
Yeah.
是啊。

886
00:31:42.270 --> 00:31:43.310
Made me laugh out loud.
让我笑出声来了。

887
00:31:43.510 --> 00:31:44.410
Yeah, so good.
是啊，太赞了。

888
00:31:44.450 --> 00:31:45.510
Like for a long time.
笑了好久。

889
00:31:45.630 --> 00:31:47.790
Yeah, and Paul's reaction is so perfect.
是啊，保罗的反应简直完美。

890
00:31:48.310 --> 00:31:52.630
In the deleted scenes, Michael goes off on him for like minutes.
在删减片段里，迈克尔足足骂了他好几分钟。

891
00:31:52.630 --> 00:32:03.330
What's so amazing is that Steve and Paul in real life are both of our kind of very gentle, quiet, kind people on the set.
最神奇的是，史蒂夫和保罗在现实生活中都是那种非常温和、安静、善良的人。

892
00:32:03.490 --> 00:32:07.310
And they have to, well, I guess just Michael has to bully Toby.
他们不得不……好吧，我想主要是迈克尔不得不欺负托比。

893
00:32:07.310 --> 00:32:12.390
But Steve and Paul's real life relationship is so opposite that.
但史蒂夫和保罗现实中的关系完全相反。

894
00:32:12.690 --> 00:32:12.830
Yeah.
是啊。

895
00:32:13.330 --> 00:32:16.310
No, but it was, oh, and Katie's like, where am I?
不，当时的情况是，噢，凯蒂一脸茫然，心想我这是在哪儿？

896
00:32:16.590 --> 00:32:18.110
Ooh, I have some Kinsey tidbits.
噢，我有一些关于金西的小花絮。

897
00:32:18.210 --> 00:32:19.010
All right, let's hear them.
好啊，说来听听。

898
00:32:19.010 --> 00:32:26.890
At eight minutes, 14 seconds, you, Pam, gets up in a huff from Roy and leaves her salad on the table.
在8分14秒的时候，你，也就是帕姆，气冲冲地从罗伊身边站起来，把沙拉留在了桌上。

899
00:32:27.330 --> 00:32:27.710
Yeah.
是啊。

900
00:32:28.190 --> 00:32:32.710
You left your, you didn't pack up your Tupperware or anything and you had a juice box.
你把东西落下了，你没收拾你的特百惠餐盒什么的，而且你还带了一盒果汁。

901
00:32:32.970 --> 00:32:35.910
What are you, I was just been, I had just been insulted.
你这是什么意思，我刚才，我刚才受了侮辱。

902
00:32:36.530 --> 00:32:37.690
He insulted me.
他侮辱了我。

903
00:32:37.830 --> 00:32:39.730
He just, he just said, we're dating.
他刚才，他刚才说我们在约会。

904
00:32:39.750 --> 00:32:41.430
And I had to say, we're not dating.
我不得不说，我们没在约会。

905
00:32:41.610 --> 00:32:42.110
We're engaged.
我们订婚了。

906
00:32:42.110 --> 00:32:43.070
I'm very hurt.
我很受伤。

907
00:32:43.350 --> 00:32:44.490
And I walk away.
然后我就走开了。

908
00:32:44.610 --> 00:32:45.210
What do you want?
你到底想怎样？

909
00:32:45.350 --> 00:32:47.450
And here's my salad and my Tupperware.
这是我的沙拉和特百惠餐盒。

910
00:32:47.750 --> 00:32:48.350
Deal with it.
自己看着办吧。

911
00:32:48.350 --> 00:32:51.750
Have you never been at a meal and been offended and just left your plate?
难道你从来没在吃饭时受过气，然后直接扔下盘子走人的吗？

912
00:32:52.010 --> 00:32:52.330
No.
没有。

913
00:32:52.970 --> 00:32:58.810
So if you're in a fight with someone over dinner, you, you get up with your plate and you go rinse
所以如果你在晚餐时和人吵架，你会，你会端着盘子起身，去把它冲洗干净

914
00:32:58.810 --> 00:32:59.930
it off and put it in the dishwasher.
然后放进洗碗机里吗？

915
00:33:00.490 --> 00:33:00.550
That's right.
没错。

916
00:33:00.650 --> 00:33:01.990
I'm going to bust my plate.
我会直接把盘子摔了。

917
00:33:02.190 --> 00:33:03.510
I'm not going to leave my salad.
我才不会留下我的沙拉。

918
00:33:03.590 --> 00:33:05.090
Well, I would love to see that.
好吧，我倒很想看看那一幕。

919
00:33:05.190 --> 00:33:05.590
Oh, well.
噢，好吧。

920
00:33:05.590 --> 00:33:08.070
I think it would have been so weird if she had taken her food with her.
我觉得如果她把食物也带走，那才叫奇怪呢。

921
00:33:09.010 --> 00:33:10.210
What an odd choice.
真是个奇怪的选择。

922
00:33:10.510 --> 00:33:15.650
I thought it was, I think it would be funny if she was mad as hell and had to pack up her salad.
我觉得，如果她气得要死还得打包沙拉，那应该会很有趣。

923
00:33:15.650 --> 00:33:19.830
I have a thing that I wanted to share about Pam's engagement ring to Roy.
关于帕姆和罗伊订婚的那枚戒指，我有一件事想分享。

924
00:33:20.090 --> 00:33:25.290
The props people, when you have to be married on a show, they'll bring you a whole tray of rings.
道具组的人，当你在剧中要结婚时，他们会拿来一整盘戒指让你选。

925
00:33:25.550 --> 00:33:25.990
To pick.
让你挑。

926
00:33:26.130 --> 00:33:26.410
Yes.
是的。

927
00:33:26.430 --> 00:33:28.590
You get to pick your engagement ring and your wedding ring.
你可以挑选你的订婚戒指和结婚戒指。

928
00:33:28.670 --> 00:33:33.830
Now, these are based on selections that have been pre-edited by the director and producers,
当然，这些都是基于导演和制片人预先筛选过的款式，

929
00:33:34.110 --> 00:33:34.250
right?
对吧？

930
00:33:34.250 --> 00:33:36.230
So you can't just pick like a honking ring.
所以你不能随便挑个大钻戒。

931
00:33:36.370 --> 00:33:36.510
Right.
没错。

932
00:33:36.570 --> 00:33:38.070
It has to match your character's life.
它必须符合你角色的生活背景。

933
00:33:38.190 --> 00:33:38.410
Yes.
是的。

934
00:33:38.510 --> 00:33:41.730
But they give you a variety of things to choose from and you have to try them on in different sizes.
但他们会提供各种各样的款式供你选择，你还得试戴不同尺寸的。

935
00:33:42.090 --> 00:33:49.550
So when they gave me the tray of rings, I picked a diamond cluster ring as opposed to a diamond
所以当他们把那盘戒指给我时，我选了一枚碎钻簇拥的戒指，而不是单颗

936
00:33:49.550 --> 00:33:50.110
solitaire.
大钻戒。

937
00:33:50.110 --> 00:34:01.630
And I had it in my mind that Pam has always been hurt that Roy didn't get her more of the ring she
我当时心里想的是，帕姆一直很受伤，因为罗伊没给她买她想要的戒指，

938
00:34:01.630 --> 00:34:06.830
wanted, which would be more of a diamond solitaire, more of what Jim is going to give her later.
她想要的是那种单颗大钻戒，更像吉姆后来会送给她的那种。

939
00:34:07.090 --> 00:34:15.610
But she's a polite person and she thinks it's not right to be offended by the ring or to not like
但她是个有礼貌的人，她觉得因为戒指而感到冒犯或者不喜欢

940
00:34:15.610 --> 00:34:15.950
the ring.
这枚戒指是不对的。

941
00:34:16.110 --> 00:34:18.250
So she had to very graciously accept this ring.
所以她必须非常优雅地接受这枚戒指。

942
00:34:18.470 --> 00:34:22.510
But I always felt like her opinion of Roy
但我一直觉得她对罗伊的看法是，

943
00:34:22.510 --> 00:34:26.410
was that he didn't put enough effort into getting to know her or what she would like,
他没有花足够的精力去了解她或者她喜欢什么，

944
00:34:26.410 --> 00:34:28.970
or he didn't put a lot of effort into the engagement ring.
或者说他在订婚戒指上没花什么心思。

945
00:34:29.210 --> 00:34:30.050
Or the relationship.
或者说是在这段关系上。

946
00:34:30.270 --> 00:34:35.690
Or the relationship, but that the ring is really a symbol of his lack of effort and his lack of
或者说是在这段关系上，但这枚戒指确实象征着他缺乏努力，也不够

947
00:34:35.690 --> 00:34:36.150
knowing her.
了解她。

948
00:34:36.290 --> 00:34:40.570
And every day when I would look down at that diamond cluster ring, it would just
每天当我低头看着那枚碎钻簇拥的戒指时，它都会

949
00:34:41.430 --> 00:34:44.550
poke at those wounds that she has in her relationship with Roy.
不断刺痛她在这段与罗伊的关系中所受的创伤。

950
00:34:44.550 --> 00:34:51.450
And so when he says boyfriend, that's another way that she's like, that's right.
所以当他说出“男朋友”这个词时，她心里的反应是，没错，就是这样。

951
00:34:51.530 --> 00:34:52.730
This ring makes
这枚戒指让我

952
00:34:52.730 --> 00:34:54.310
me feel like we're not engaged.
感觉我们好像没订婚一样。

953
00:34:54.550 --> 00:34:58.250
I've been wearing this diamond cluster ring for three years and it
这枚碎钻戒指我已经戴了三年了，它

954
00:34:58.250 --> 00:35:00.110
feels like a thing that you give your girlfriend.
感觉像是送给女朋友的东西。

955
00:35:00.350 --> 00:35:02.190
It doesn't feel like what you give someone
它感觉不像是在求婚时

956
00:35:02.190 --> 00:35:05.570
when you're proposing, at least for Pam.
送给别人的东西，至少对帕姆来说是这样。

957
00:35:05.830 --> 00:35:06.730
Does that make sense?
这说得通吗？

958
00:35:06.950 --> 00:35:07.330
It does.
说得通。

959
00:35:07.430 --> 00:35:09.090
And it also just makes me sad.
而且它也让我感到难过。

960
00:35:09.270 --> 00:35:12.710
And now I take back my salad, my salad judgment.
现在我收回我的沙拉，关于沙拉的评价。

961
00:35:12.710 --> 00:35:13.970
See how hurt she was.
看她当时有多受伤。

