肯定会有人受伤的。

1137
00:40:28.290 --> 00:40:32.830
That was the difficulty for me in that scene because tickling me makes me irritated.
那场戏对我来说很难，因为被挠痒痒会让我很烦躁。

1138
00:40:33.110 --> 00:40:33.890
Want to whack someone.
想揍人。

1139
00:40:34.110 --> 00:40:35.470
Does not make me laugh.
并不会让我发笑。

1140
00:40:36.210 --> 00:40:39.470
Well, I thought you did a great job and it was cringy as heck.
嗯，我觉得你演得很好，尴尬得要命。

1141
00:40:39.570 --> 00:40:39.730
Yeah.
是啊。

1142
00:40:39.730 --> 00:40:40.130
Poor Jim.
可怜的吉姆。

1143
00:40:40.330 --> 00:40:40.730
I know.
我知道。

1144
00:40:40.910 --> 00:40:41.170
All right.
好吧。

1145
00:40:41.250 --> 00:40:41.990
We're going to go to a break.
我们要进广告了。

1146
00:40:42.110 --> 00:40:42.790
Let's take a break.
休息一下吧。

1147
00:40:52.850 --> 00:40:55.910
Angela, I want to start by asking you a question.
安吉拉，我想先问你一个问题。

1148
00:40:56.290 --> 00:40:56.490
Okay.
好的。

1149
00:40:56.830 --> 00:41:02.250
You know the scene where Dwight is asking Katie on the date and it's in front of your character
你知道德怀特约凯蒂出去的那场戏吗？就在你角色的面前，

1150
00:41:02.250 --> 00:41:03.590
because you're looking at purses?
因为你当时正在看包包？

1151
00:41:03.590 --> 00:41:03.970
Mm-hmm.
嗯。

1152
00:41:04.350 --> 00:41:08.850
Your face during that moment, what were you thinking?
那一刻你的表情，你在想什么？

1153
00:41:09.330 --> 00:41:10.810
I did not even look up.
我甚至都没有抬头。

1154
00:41:11.010 --> 00:41:11.310
No.
没有。

1155
00:41:11.450 --> 00:41:12.690
You just kept your eyes down.
你只是低着头。

1156
00:41:12.830 --> 00:41:16.390
I kept my eyes down and then I didn't look up until he walked out of the room.
我一直低着头，直到他走出房间我才抬头。

1157
00:41:16.510 --> 00:41:20.070
And you can see when he exits, I kind of look up and look at him leave.
你可以看到他离开时，我稍微抬起头看着他走掉。

1158
00:41:20.330 --> 00:41:23.570
You know, in that moment, it was so awkward and uncomfortable.
你知道，那一刻真的太尴尬、太不自在了。

1159
00:41:23.570 --> 00:41:26.870
I wasn't given direction to do that, but I just felt so uncomfortable.
导演并没有要求我那样做，但我就是觉得很不自在。

1160
00:41:26.870 --> 00:41:28.330
I just kept looking down.
我只能一直低着头。

1161
00:41:28.550 --> 00:41:30.650
But Dwight is not a thing yet.
但那时候德怀特和安吉拉还没成一对呢。

1162
00:41:30.770 --> 00:41:31.050
No.
没错。

1163
00:41:31.230 --> 00:41:35.990
But it is so easy to superimpose what we know is going to happen between your two characters
但我们很容易把后来你们两个角色之间会发生的事，

1164
00:41:35.990 --> 00:41:37.290
onto this moment.
投射到那一刻。

1165
00:41:37.370 --> 00:41:42.670
But people were asking if you knew that your characters were going to end up together in
人们都在问，在那一刻你是否已经知道你们的角色最终会走到一起，

1166
00:41:42.670 --> 00:41:44.410
that moment yet, but you didn't, right?
但你当时并不知道，对吧？

1167
00:41:44.410 --> 00:41:45.150
I didn't know.
我不知道。

1168
00:41:45.270 --> 00:41:45.810
I didn't know.
我不知道。

1169
00:41:45.930 --> 00:41:49.030
And just in that conference room, it's not a huge space.
而且就在那个会议室里，空间并不大。

1170
00:41:49.210 --> 00:41:54.890
And him putting himself out there like that to her, I, as Angela, and even as myself, felt
他那样向她表露心迹，作为安吉拉，甚至作为我自己，我都感到

1171
00:41:54.890 --> 00:42:00.190
so uncomfortable that I just was trying somehow not to participate in the moment in any way.
非常不自在，所以我只是想方设法不参与到那一刻中去。

1172
00:42:00.350 --> 00:42:01.430
Like try to just be invisible?
就像是想让自己隐形一样？

1173
00:42:01.430 --> 00:42:01.730
Yeah.
是的。

1174
00:42:01.950 --> 00:42:03.810
I was, in my mind, I was like, just be invisible.
我在心里想的就是，让自己隐形吧。

1175
00:42:04.190 --> 00:42:07.810
I think that, you know, Angela didn't know that Dwight was going to be her soulmate,
我觉得，你知道，安吉拉当时并不知道德怀特会成为她的灵魂伴侣，

1176
00:42:07.890 --> 00:42:09.990
but I think she did see him as an equal.
但我认为她确实把他视为平等的存在。

1177
00:42:09.990 --> 00:42:14.730
And she respected his work ethic and probably respected who he was in the office, even though
她尊重他的职业道德，也可能尊重他在办公室里的为人，尽管

1178
00:42:14.730 --> 00:42:16.030
he annoyed her, right?
他让她感到厌烦，对吧？

1179
00:42:16.170 --> 00:42:16.450
Sure.
当然。

1180
00:42:16.650 --> 00:42:18.530
There was a power struggle between the two of them.
他们两人之间存在着权力斗争。

1181
00:42:18.650 --> 00:42:24.490
So to see him sort of humble himself like that to Katie and get humiliated, I just felt
所以看到他那样在凯蒂面前放低姿态却遭到羞辱，我当时觉得

1182
00:42:24.490 --> 00:42:27.270
like I didn't even want him to think that I had witnessed it.
我甚至不想让他觉得我目睹了这一切。

1183
00:42:27.530 --> 00:42:28.550
I didn't see it.
我没看见。

1184
00:42:28.650 --> 00:42:29.370
It didn't happen.
这事儿没发生过。

1185
00:42:29.510 --> 00:42:29.930
It's okay.
没关系的。

1186
00:42:29.930 --> 00:42:32.030
That's, I think, what she was thinking.
我想这就是她当时的想法。

1187
00:42:32.230 --> 00:42:33.670
And that's why I didn't look up.
这就是我为什么没有抬头的原因。

1188
00:42:33.790 --> 00:42:35.890
I was literally trying to be invisible in the moment.
那一刻我真的在努力让自己隐形。

1189
00:42:36.210 --> 00:42:41.170
Well, after that, you have a line that is one of my favorite lines of your character
嗯，在那之后，你有一句台词是我最喜欢你这个角色的台词之一，

1190
00:42:41.170 --> 00:42:42.970
where you describe your favorite colors.
就是你描述你最喜欢的颜色那段。

1191
00:42:43.670 --> 00:42:45.370
This is a fan question from Emmy.
这是一个来自艾米的粉丝提问。

1192
00:42:45.530 --> 00:42:49.390
Angela, did you improvise the scene where you discuss your colors being different shades
安吉拉，你讨论自己喜欢的颜色是不同深浅的灰色那场戏，

1193
00:42:49.390 --> 00:42:49.830
of gray?
是即兴发挥的吗？

1194
00:42:50.130 --> 00:42:50.810
Yes, I did.
是的，是我即兴发挥的。

1195
00:42:50.930 --> 00:42:51.770
I knew it.
我就知道。

1196
00:42:51.930 --> 00:42:52.490
Yes, I did.
是的，是我发挥的。

1197
00:42:52.670 --> 00:42:58.170
In the episode, Dwight is looking in at the conference room at Katie and Angela sort of
在那一集里，德怀特正往会议室里看，看着凯蒂和安吉拉在

1198
00:42:58.170 --> 00:43:00.410
talking, and we didn't have any scripted dialogue.
聊天，我们当时没有任何剧本台词。

1199
00:43:00.410 --> 00:43:02.230
So they said, can you just kind of banter?
所以他们说，你们能随便聊几句吗？

1200
00:43:02.410 --> 00:43:05.150
And I didn't even know if it would make it in, you know?
我甚至不知道这段会不会被剪进正片里，你知道吗？

1201
00:43:05.350 --> 00:43:07.490
And so that scene was improvised.
所以那一幕是即兴发挥的。

1202
00:43:07.550 --> 00:43:11.810
And it starts off with Amy as Katie saying, well, you seem to like to touch things.
开头是艾米饰演的凯蒂说，嗯，你好像很喜欢摸东西。

1203
00:43:12.270 --> 00:43:16.330
And then I just responded, I don't like to necessarily touch things.
然后我回应说，我不一定喜欢摸东西。

1204
00:43:16.330 --> 00:43:17.590
I'm shopping, you know?
我是在购物，你懂吗？

1205
00:43:17.730 --> 00:43:18.550
I loved that line.
我很喜欢那句台词。

1206
00:43:18.710 --> 00:43:20.390
And then she said, well, what color do you like?
然后她说，好吧，那你喜欢什么颜色？

1207
00:43:20.450 --> 00:43:21.430
And this was all improvised.
这些全都是即兴发挥的。

1208
00:43:21.530 --> 00:43:24.410
And I said, gray, dark gray, charcoal.
我说，灰色，深灰色，炭灰色。

1209
00:43:25.170 --> 00:43:26.750
And it made it in.
结果那句台词被保留了下来。

1210
00:43:26.830 --> 00:43:27.790
And that was really fun.
那真的很有趣。

1211
00:43:27.950 --> 00:43:30.990
And then that line ended up in an article in the newspaper.
后来那句台词还上了一篇报纸文章。

1212
00:43:30.990 --> 00:43:33.650
It was talking about what sums up the show.
文章在讨论什么能概括这部剧。

1213
00:43:33.790 --> 00:43:39.110
And they said, well, the character Angela's line, gray, dark gray, charcoal, really sets
他们说，安吉拉这个角色的台词“灰色，深灰色，炭灰色”，真的奠定了

1214
00:43:39.110 --> 00:43:39.690
the tone.
整部剧的基调。

1215
00:43:39.870 --> 00:43:41.430
And I was so proud of that.
我对此感到非常自豪。

1216
00:43:41.810 --> 00:43:45.710
It really then informed a lot of your wardrobe after that.
那之后确实影响了你大部分的服装选择。

1217
00:43:45.910 --> 00:43:50.770
You had been kind of wearing these muted colors, but that became your uniform moving forward.
你本来就穿这些柔和的颜色，但那之后这就成了你的标配。

1218
00:43:51.070 --> 00:43:52.470
Okay, Jenna, what else do you have?
好的，珍娜，你还有什么？

1219
00:43:52.610 --> 00:43:52.950
All right.
好的。

1220
00:43:53.170 --> 00:43:58.430
The scene where Ryan and Michael are cleaning out his car, that was not improvised.
瑞安和迈克尔清理他车子的那一幕，那不是即兴发挥的。

1221
00:43:58.590 --> 00:43:59.490
No, that was scripted.
不，那是写在剧本里的。

1222
00:43:59.570 --> 00:44:05.690
A lot of people asked, all of it, blue blast, smell alike, how many filet of fish do you
很多人问，所有的那些，蓝色冲击，气味一样，你吃了多少个麦香鱼，

1223
00:44:05.690 --> 00:44:07.410
All of those lines are in the script.
所有这些台词都在剧本里。

1224
00:44:07.690 --> 00:44:12.430
I checked because when I was watching it, it was so hard for me to believe that it was
我特意查了一下，因为我在看的时候，很难相信那不是

1225
00:44:12.430 --> 00:44:15.310
not improvised that I went back to my script and I read it.
即兴发挥的，所以我回去翻了剧本读了一遍。

1226
00:44:15.430 --> 00:44:20.290
And I think that it just points to how good the writing was on our show.
我觉得这恰恰说明了我们剧的剧本有多棒。

1227
00:44:20.610 --> 00:44:20.770
Fantastic.
太棒了。

1228
00:44:21.150 --> 00:44:22.110
Just how good.
就是那么棒。

1229
00:44:22.250 --> 00:44:24.730
And also how good the actors were.
还有演员们也演得非常好。

1230
00:44:25.210 --> 00:44:30.910
I mean, BJ and Steve in that scene, just absolutely brilliant.
我是说，BJ和史蒂夫在那一幕里的表演简直绝了。

1231
00:44:30.910 --> 00:44:36.610
Mindy also told me that the reference to the filet of fishes is a nod to her disgusting
明迪还告诉我，提到麦香鱼其实是在致敬她现实生活中对麦香鱼那种

1232
00:44:36.610 --> 00:44:38.250
love of filet of fish in real life.
令人作呕的喜爱。

1233
00:44:38.330 --> 00:44:40.070
Or just her love for McDonald's.
或者说她对麦当劳的喜爱。

1234
00:44:40.190 --> 00:44:41.810
She loves McDonald's.
她很爱麦当劳。

1235
00:44:43.070 --> 00:44:45.610
But that she really does love a filet of fish.
但她是真的非常喜欢麦香鱼。

1236
00:44:45.750 --> 00:44:51.890
I loved in this scene too when Michael's like, that was over a period of time, okay?
我也很喜欢这一幕，当迈克尔说，那是一段时间内积累的，好吗？

1237
00:44:51.890 --> 00:44:52.690
It was over a month.
那是一个月的时间。

1238
00:44:52.750 --> 00:44:53.450
It was over a month.
那是一个月的时间。

1239
00:44:53.770 --> 00:44:55.610
And Ryan the Temp goes, still.
然后临时工瑞安说，那也一样。

1240
00:44:55.930 --> 00:44:56.210
Yeah.
没错。

1241
00:44:57.270 --> 00:44:59.350
I could watch that scene over and over again.
那一幕我可以反复看上无数遍。

1242
00:44:59.350 --> 00:45:00.350
I think that's a gem.
我觉得那是个珍品。

1243
00:45:00.570 --> 00:45:03.830
I think if you haven't rewatched this episode, but you're listening to the podcast,
如果你还没重温过这一集，但正在听播客的话，

1244
00:45:04.130 --> 00:45:05.770
just please go watch that scene.
请一定要去看看那一幕。

1245
00:45:05.930 --> 00:45:06.510
It's so good.
真的太棒了。

1246
00:45:06.850 --> 00:45:08.070
Blue is not a flavor.
蓝色不是一种口味。

1247
00:45:09.110 --> 00:45:10.190
I have a note card.
我有一张笔记卡。

1248
00:45:10.410 --> 00:45:10.990
Say it.
说出来。

1249
00:45:11.230 --> 00:45:11.530
Okay.
好的。

1250
00:45:11.690 --> 00:45:14.550
This is a great, great Dwight line when he says,
这是德怀特一句非常非常棒的台词，他说，

1251
00:45:14.890 --> 00:45:16.790
Shrutes produce very thirsty babies.
施鲁特家族的孩子都很渴。

1252
00:45:17.010 --> 00:45:17.930
Oh, yes.
噢，没错。

1253
00:45:18.110 --> 00:45:19.150
That's a famous line.
那可是句名台词。

1254
00:45:19.270 --> 00:45:20.170
That's a famous line.
那可是句名台词。

1255
00:45:20.290 --> 00:45:23.410
And when I was pregnant, I was pregnant season five of The Office.
我怀孕的时候，正好是《办公室》第五季拍摄期间。

1256
00:45:23.550 --> 00:45:26.630
And I got a gift of a t-shirt that said,
我收到了一件T恤作为礼物，上面写着：

1257
00:45:26.870 --> 00:45:29.010
Shrutes produce very thirsty babies.
施鲁特家族的孩子都很渴。

1258
00:45:29.010 --> 00:45:30.470
And it was a maternity shirt.
那是一件孕妇装。

1259
00:45:30.690 --> 00:45:31.430
Oh, my God.
天哪。

1260
00:45:31.650 --> 00:45:35.570
And I wore that around my big belly and people would freak out.
我挺着大肚子穿上它，人们看到都会大吃一惊。

1261
00:45:35.770 --> 00:45:36.630
I still have it.
我现在还留着它。

1262
00:45:36.730 --> 00:45:37.410
I still have it.
我现在还留着它。

1263
00:45:37.670 --> 00:45:37.910
Oh.
噢。

1264
00:45:38.230 --> 00:45:39.630
Do you have a picture of yourself in that?
你有穿那件衣服的照片吗？

1265
00:45:39.950 --> 00:45:40.630
I will look.
我找找看。

1266
00:45:40.690 --> 00:45:43.230
But if I don't, I'll just take a picture of myself in it.
如果找不到，我就自己穿上拍一张。

1267
00:45:43.370 --> 00:45:46.550
And I'll have to post that on Office Ladies Pod because I still have that shirt.
然后我得把它发到《办公室女士》播客上，因为我确实还留着那件衣服。

1268
00:45:46.730 --> 00:45:47.150
You should.
你应该发。

1269
00:45:47.270 --> 00:45:47.510
Definitely.
绝对应该。

1270
00:45:47.930 --> 00:45:50.490
Here is something that everybody wrote in about.
这是大家写信问得最多的一个问题。

1271
00:45:50.610 --> 00:45:52.390
This was one of our most popular questions.
这是我们收到的最热门的问题之一。

1272
00:45:53.030 --> 00:45:56.630
What's up with the wrong parking lot at the end of this episode?
这集结尾的停车场怎么不对劲？

1273
00:45:56.850 --> 00:46:00.530
That's because this was the original set before we moved.
那是因为在我们搬迁之前，那是最初的片场。

1274
00:46:00.530 --> 00:46:04.850
The first six episodes, we all filmed at an actual office building in Culver City.
前六集我们都是在卡尔弗城的一栋真实办公楼里拍摄的。

1275
00:46:04.910 --> 00:46:06.070
And that was the parking lot.
那就是当时的停车场。

1276
00:46:06.250 --> 00:46:06.570
Yes.
没错。

1277
00:46:06.570 --> 00:46:10.650
So when we moved in season two and beyond, we had two soundstages.
所以从第二季开始，我们搬到了两个摄影棚。

1278
00:46:10.810 --> 00:46:17.270
One soundstage was a recreation of the office, that interior office that we shot in the first year.
一个摄影棚是第一年拍摄时那个室内办公室的复刻版。

1279
00:46:17.690 --> 00:46:20.230
The other building is where the writers worked.
另一栋楼是编剧们工作的地方。

1280
00:46:20.330 --> 00:46:21.570
And it was just an office building.
那只是一栋普通的办公楼。

1281
00:46:21.570 --> 00:46:23.650
And that was just the parking lot for it.
那只是那栋楼的停车场。

1282
00:46:23.770 --> 00:46:24.170
Yes.
是的。

1283
00:46:24.330 --> 00:46:27.690
And that is where we filmed the Dunder Mifflin parking lot.
那就是我们拍摄邓德·米福林停车场的地方。

1284
00:46:27.690 --> 00:46:32.950
So it was really interesting because we had our warehouse set over there.
所以这很有趣，因为我们的仓库布景在那边。

1285
00:46:33.270 --> 00:46:35.070
And then we had the parking lot.
然后我们有停车场。

1286
00:46:35.250 --> 00:46:37.790
And we had the lobby and the elevator where Hank's at.
还有大厅和汉克所在的电梯。

1287
00:46:37.970 --> 00:46:38.290
Yes.
没错。

1288
00:46:38.450 --> 00:46:39.750
All of that was one building.
所有这些都在同一栋楼里。

1289
00:46:39.750 --> 00:46:42.050
But then the Dunder Mifflin building was something else.
但邓德·米福林大楼是另一回事。

1290
00:46:42.090 --> 00:46:46.110
So if we had to do a scene where you see us walk out,
所以如果我们拍一场戏，需要看到我们走出来，

1291
00:46:46.150 --> 00:46:53.970
we would have to start that scene in one building and then move all the cameras and all of us over to the other building and then get the exterior version of it.
我们就得在一栋楼里开始拍摄，然后把所有摄像机和所有人都搬到另一栋楼，再拍摄外景部分。

1292
00:46:54.130 --> 00:46:54.530
Yes.
没错。

1293
00:46:54.610 --> 00:46:55.490
It was quite complicated.
这相当复杂。

1294
00:46:55.490 --> 00:47:02.190
It was basically when we filmed in one stage indoors, we filmed another stage outdoors for the most part.
基本上就是我们在一个摄影棚拍室内戏时，大部分时间都要在另一个摄影棚拍室外戏。

1295
00:47:02.350 --> 00:47:08.470
But that parking lot is not the Dunder Mifflin parking lot that you see from season two and beyond.
但那个停车场并不是你在第二季及之后看到的邓德·米福林停车场。

1296
00:47:08.730 --> 00:47:10.690
And I have a story about that parking lot.
关于那个停车场，我有个故事要讲。

1297
00:47:10.870 --> 00:47:17.210
You see in that final shot, it starts with Michael and Jim and Katie leaving.
你看最后那个镜头，迈克尔、吉姆和凯蒂正准备离开。

1298
00:47:17.610 --> 00:47:18.630
She's got her big bag.
她背着个大包。

1299
00:47:18.850 --> 00:47:22.950
Michael realizes that Jim is going to be giving her a ride home because they're going to get drinks.
迈克尔意识到吉姆要送她回家，因为他们要去喝一杯。

1300
00:47:22.950 --> 00:47:30.930
And then it reveals Pam and Roy backing up in Roy's truck and Pam clocks Jim and Katie.
然后镜头转到帕姆和罗伊，他们正倒车开着罗伊的卡车，帕姆注意到了吉姆和凯蒂。

1301
00:47:31.950 --> 00:47:43.250
So David and I had to sit in that truck in the parking lot and wait a very long time until everyone came out and did that scene and we had a little walkie-talkie inside the truck and they would say,
所以大卫和我不得不坐在停车场的那辆卡车里，等了很长时间，直到所有人都出来拍完那场戏，我们车里有个小对讲机，他们会说，

1302
00:47:43.410 --> 00:47:43.570
go.
开始。

1303
00:47:43.930 --> 00:47:49.990
And then David would back up and we would pull out and the camera would get that shot of me looking sad and we would drive off.
然后大卫会倒车，我们开出去，摄像机拍下我看起来很伤心的镜头，然后我们就开车离开。

1304
00:47:50.110 --> 00:47:51.150
And then they would say, reset.
接着他们会说，重置。

1305
00:47:51.490 --> 00:47:54.750
And we would bring the truck back and then we would wait a very long time.
我们就把卡车开回去，然后又要等很长时间。

1306
00:47:55.470 --> 00:48:04.150
At the end of the night, they reset us back into the parking lot and we sat there and we sat there in the truck.
那天晚上结束时，他们让我们回到停车场，我们就坐在那儿，坐在卡车里。

1307
00:48:04.410 --> 00:48:11.150
We sat there in the truck and then all of a sudden, we saw everyone driving away in their own cars.
我们坐在卡车里，突然间，我们看到大家都开着自己的车走了。

1308
00:48:11.390 --> 00:48:12.050
Oh, no!
噢，不！

1309
00:48:12.470 --> 00:48:14.310
They left us in the truck.
他们把我们留在卡车里了。

1310
00:48:14.490 --> 00:48:16.870
They forgot to tell us that they had wrapped.
他们忘了告诉我们已经收工了。

1311
00:48:17.290 --> 00:48:18.010
Oh, Jenna.
噢，珍娜。

1312
00:48:18.010 --> 00:48:18.590
For the day.
当天的拍摄。

1313
00:48:18.850 --> 00:48:20.630
And we were all done and we were leaving.
我们都拍完了，大家都要走了。

1314
00:48:20.630 --> 00:48:21.490
You were done.
你们拍完了。

1315
00:48:21.810 --> 00:48:23.190
You were changing clothes.
你们在换衣服。

1316
00:48:23.430 --> 00:48:25.070
You were getting in your cars.
你们在坐进各自的车里。

1317
00:48:25.070 --> 00:48:26.750
We saw the director leave.
我们看到导演离开了。

1318
00:48:26.990 --> 00:48:28.130
We saw actors leave.
我们看到演员们离开了。

1319
00:48:28.470 --> 00:48:30.430
David and I were like, what?
大卫和我当时就想，什么？

1320
00:48:30.750 --> 00:48:31.250
What?
什么？

1321
00:48:31.250 --> 00:48:32.250
What is going on?
到底怎么回事？

1322
00:48:33.070 --> 00:48:34.910
So, and here's the thing.
所以，重点是这个。

1323
00:48:35.070 --> 00:48:36.490
I've talked about this before.
我以前说过这件事。

1324
00:48:36.750 --> 00:48:39.530
David Denman and I were very good friends in real life.
大卫·丹曼和我在现实生活中是非常好的朋友。

1325
00:48:39.670 --> 00:48:47.270
We talked about in the basketball episode how you and I became best friends because we had to sit on that bench for hours and hours.
我们在聊篮球那一集时提到过，你和我成了最好的朋友，因为我们不得不坐在那张长椅上好几个小时。

1326
00:48:47.970 --> 00:48:51.370
This is really the episode where David and I became such good friends.
这一集真的是大卫和我成为好朋友的契机。

1327
00:48:51.550 --> 00:48:53.550
Well, you had a lot of like St. Louis connections.
嗯，你们有很多关于圣路易斯的联系。

1328
00:48:53.730 --> 00:48:54.050
We did.
确实有。

1329
00:48:54.430 --> 00:48:54.690
You had mutual friends.
你们有共同的朋友。

1330
00:48:54.990 --> 00:48:56.630
And we had the poker connection.
而且我们还有扑克牌的交情。

1331
00:48:56.870 --> 00:48:57.290
Yes.
没错。

1332
00:48:57.570 --> 00:49:00.990
David and I played in a poker game together with our crew.
大卫和我跟我们的剧组人员一起玩过扑克。

1333
00:49:01.270 --> 00:49:02.870
We would host these poker games.
我们会组织这些扑克局。

1334
00:49:02.990 --> 00:49:04.010
Rain was in on it.
雷恩也参与其中。

1335
00:49:04.550 --> 00:49:07.150
Chris Workman, who was one of our camera operators.
克里斯·沃克曼，我们的摄像师之一。

1336
00:49:07.990 --> 00:49:09.570
Ed, our camera assistant.
艾德，我们的摄像助理。

1337
00:49:09.670 --> 00:49:12.350
We would all get together and we would play poker.
我们大家会聚在一起玩扑克。

1338
00:49:12.770 --> 00:49:14.130
And he was part of that.
他也是其中的一员。

1339
00:49:14.250 --> 00:49:15.530
So, he was one of my poker pals.
所以，他是我的牌友之一。

1340
00:49:16.250 --> 00:49:22.190
And anyway, this was the episode where we really became friends because we got left in that truck.
总之，这一集是我们真正成为朋友的契机，因为我们被留在了那辆卡车里。

1341
00:49:22.450 --> 00:49:23.430
You got stuck in that truck.
你们被困在那辆卡车里了。

1342
00:49:23.750 --> 00:49:24.390
Jenna, do you know what?
珍娜，你知道吗？

1343
00:49:24.430 --> 00:49:29.470
I'm seeing a theme here that you become really close friends with people that you are in a confined space with.
我发现了一个主题，就是你总是会和那些跟你待在狭窄空间里的人成为好朋友。

1344
00:49:29.530 --> 00:49:30.850
That I get stuck with.
那些我被困住的人。

1345
00:49:31.170 --> 00:49:31.870
You're stuck on a bench.
你被困在长椅上。

1346
00:49:31.970 --> 00:49:33.030
I'll be Angela's best friend.
我就会成为安吉拉最好的朋友。

1347
00:49:33.050 --> 00:49:34.030
I'm stuck in a truck.
我被困在卡车里。

1348
00:49:34.210 --> 00:49:35.090
David, let's play poker.
大卫，我们来玩扑克吧。

1349
00:49:36.170 --> 00:49:38.070
Get stuck in an elevator with me.
跟我一起被困在电梯里吧。

1350
00:49:38.230 --> 00:49:39.770
And then you're going to be best friends.
然后你就会成为我最好的朋友。

1351
00:49:39.830 --> 00:49:40.690
Friends for life.
一辈子的朋友。

1352
00:49:40.930 --> 00:49:42.710
I have my final note card.
我还有最后一张笔记卡。

1353
00:49:43.110 --> 00:49:43.310
Ready?
准备好了吗？

1354
00:49:43.610 --> 00:49:44.010
Yes.
好了。

1355
00:49:44.010 --> 00:49:44.850
All right.
好极了。

1356
00:49:45.250 --> 00:49:57.230
At around 21 minutes, 25 seconds, you see both Meredith, played by Kate Flannery, and Meredith, played by Henriette, in the same episode.
在大约21分25秒的时候，你会看到凯特·弗兰纳里饰演的梅雷迪思和亨丽埃特饰演的梅雷迪思出现在同一集里。

1357
00:49:57.310 --> 00:49:57.810
Yes!
没错！

1358
00:49:57.930 --> 00:49:59.070
You saw it, Angela!
你看到了，安吉拉！

1359
00:49:59.070 --> 00:49:59.390
Yes!
没错！

1360
00:49:59.570 --> 00:50:02.190
I saw it and I almost texted you.
我看到了，当时差点就给你发短信了。

1361
00:50:02.590 --> 00:50:03.870
Background expert.
背景专家。

1362
00:50:04.310 --> 00:50:07.810
But I thought, no, I'm going to wait and see if she sees it.
但我心想，不行，我要等等看她能不能发现。

1363
00:50:07.870 --> 00:50:09.490
Yes, this is a huge mistake.
没错，这是一个巨大的失误。

1364
00:50:09.790 --> 00:50:10.590
It's a huge mistake.
这真是个巨大的失误。

1365
00:50:10.590 --> 00:50:16.270
So basically, while Michael has this talking head, they want to show all these clips of different women in the office.
所以基本上，在迈克尔进行这段采访时，他们想展示办公室里不同女性的片段。

1366
00:50:16.270 --> 00:50:23.130
And they used, like, some footage from the pilot before Kate Flannery came on.
他们用了凯特·弗兰纳里加入之前试播集里的一些镜头。

1367
00:50:23.190 --> 00:50:24.390
And it was Henriette as Meredith.
那是亨丽埃特饰演的梅雷迪思。

1368
00:50:24.590 --> 00:50:30.110
You have this montage that goes Kate Flannery to Henriette to Luanne, who played in the Annex.
你看到的蒙太奇镜头里，先是凯特·弗兰纳里，接着是亨丽埃特，然后是卢安，她在附楼里演过戏。

1369
00:50:30.110 --> 00:50:32.370
Who was one of our extras for a very long time.
她做了我们很长一段时间的临时演员。

1370
00:50:32.370 --> 00:50:33.290
So that makes sense.
所以这就说得通了。

1371
00:50:33.750 --> 00:50:36.610
I saw that and I got so excited for you.
我看到那个的时候，为你感到特别兴奋。

1372
00:50:36.610 --> 00:50:37.690
I got so excited.
我太兴奋了。

1373
00:50:37.950 --> 00:50:38.770
Because you knew.
因为你知道。

1374
00:50:38.890 --> 00:50:40.230
I knew you were going to clock it.
我就知道你会发现的。

1375
00:50:40.350 --> 00:50:41.910
You knew I had my note card ready.
你知道我准备好了笔记卡。

1376
00:50:42.150 --> 00:50:44.970
I have a final little tidbit.
我还有一个最后的小花絮。

1377
00:50:45.230 --> 00:50:46.970
I have a Fisher tidbit.
我有一个关于费舍尔的花絮。

1378
00:50:47.170 --> 00:50:48.030
The coffee maker.
那个咖啡机。

1379
00:50:48.250 --> 00:50:50.650
We never find out who won the coffee maker.
我们从来没发现到底是谁赢了咖啡机。

1380
00:50:50.870 --> 00:50:51.350
No.
没有。

1381
00:50:51.930 --> 00:50:54.190
I'm feeling like I need to know.
我觉得我必须得知道。

1382
00:50:54.370 --> 00:50:57.190
We never find out who won it and we never see it again.
我们从来没发现是谁赢了它，也再没见过它。

1383
00:50:57.370 --> 00:50:57.690
We never see it again.
我们再也没见过它。

1384
00:50:57.690 --> 00:50:58.810
So it doesn't stay in the office.
所以它并没有留在办公室。

1385
00:50:59.390 --> 00:51:02.210
I asked Phil Shea because a fan wrote in.
我问了菲尔·谢伊，因为有粉丝写信来问。

1386
00:51:02.310 --> 00:51:04.490
They wanted to know, did any of us get to keep it?
他们想知道，我们中有没有人能把它留下来？

1387
00:51:04.590 --> 00:51:07.590
People are very interested in the things we're allowed to keep and not keep.
大家对我们能留什么、不能留什么非常感兴趣。

1388
00:51:07.710 --> 00:51:08.170
I get it.
我理解。

1389
00:51:08.770 --> 00:51:09.990
He said no.
他说没有。

1390
00:51:10.390 --> 00:51:14.990
He said it was borrowed from Starbucks and had to be returned.
他说那是从星巴克借来的，必须归还。

1391
00:51:15.470 --> 00:51:16.450
I believe that.
我相信这一点。

1392
00:51:16.450 --> 00:51:17.870
Where is that machine now?
那台机器现在在哪儿？

1393
00:51:17.970 --> 00:51:19.070
I actually believe that.
我确实相信这一点。

1394
00:51:19.090 --> 00:51:23.450
And I bet the purses were returned because we were on a tight budget and we thought we
我敢打赌那些包也归还了，因为我们当时预算很紧，而且我们以为

1395
00:51:23.450 --> 00:51:24.290
were getting canceled.
我们快要被砍了。

1396
00:51:24.490 --> 00:51:24.650
Yes.
没错。

1397
00:51:24.670 --> 00:51:28.190
And we didn't want to give NBC any reason to think we were trouble.
我们不想给NBC任何理由认为我们是个麻烦。

1398
00:51:28.650 --> 00:51:29.070
That's right.
说得对。

1399
00:51:29.270 --> 00:51:33.250
So I think, I believe that all of that was returned and we got to recoup that money.
所以我认为，我相信所有那些东西都归还了，我们得以收回那笔钱。

1400
00:51:33.410 --> 00:51:34.150
For sure.
肯定的。

1401
00:51:34.450 --> 00:51:37.370
Well, Jenna, I think that was some really fun fast facts.
好吧，珍娜，我觉得这些速览小知识真的很有趣。

1402
00:51:37.470 --> 00:51:38.570
You did a great job.
你做得太棒了。

1403
00:51:38.930 --> 00:51:39.270
Wow.
哇。

1404
00:51:39.450 --> 00:51:39.910
Thank you.
谢谢。

1405
00:51:40.450 --> 00:51:41.170
You're welcome.
不客气。

1406
00:51:41.170 --> 00:51:43.130
I really appreciate it, Angela.
安吉拉，我真的很感激。

1407
00:51:43.410 --> 00:51:43.950
Oh, no, no, no.
噢，不，不，不。

1408
00:51:43.950 --> 00:51:44.490
I think.
我想是吧。

1409
00:51:44.830 --> 00:51:49.870
Now I need to hear you sing because if that's what you sound like, I just realized we've
现在我得听听你唱歌了，因为如果这就是你的歌声，我刚意识到我们

1410
00:51:49.870 --> 00:51:52.510
never like done karaoke or anything together.
从来没一起去唱过卡拉OK什么的。

1411
00:51:52.510 --> 00:51:59.730
On the wings of love, only the two of us together fly and hide.
在爱的羽翼上，只有我们俩一起飞翔躲藏。

1412
00:51:59.850 --> 00:52:00.630
Okay, don't sing anymore.
好了，别再唱了。

1413
00:52:00.630 --> 00:52:01.590
We'll have to pay for it.
我们得为此付出代价的。

1414
00:52:02.990 --> 00:52:06.370
But now I know you're, now I have got your karaoke voice.
但现在我知道了，现在我听到了你的卡拉OK嗓音。

1415
00:52:06.510 --> 00:52:07.750
And it's whispery.
而且是耳语般的。

1416
00:52:08.230 --> 00:52:09.070
It's whispery.
是耳语般的。

1417
00:52:09.070 --> 00:52:10.370
Well, I'm trying to cover up my floss.
好吧，我是在掩饰我的牙线。

1418
00:52:10.690 --> 00:52:13.370
And if you can't really sing, you whisper sing.
如果你真的不会唱歌，你就会耳语式演唱。

1419
00:52:13.930 --> 00:52:15.130
And that was Hot Girl.
以上就是《辣妹》那一集。

1420
00:52:15.310 --> 00:52:16.690
And that wraps up season one.
第一季到此结束。

1421
00:52:16.690 --> 00:52:19.290
Season one, where you and I become best friends.
第一季，你和我成为了最好的朋友。

1422
00:52:19.290 --> 00:52:19.570
Yes.
没错。

1423
00:52:19.810 --> 00:52:21.270
Because you were stuck on a bench with me.
因为你被困在长椅上和我在一起。

1424
00:52:21.490 --> 00:52:21.630
Yeah.
是啊。

1425
00:52:21.810 --> 00:52:24.390
And where you also became friends with someone because you were stuck in a car with them.
还有你和某人也成为了朋友，因为你被困在车里和他们在一起。

1426
00:52:24.550 --> 00:52:24.730
Yeah.
是啊。

1427
00:52:24.910 --> 00:52:25.710
See a pattern here.
看出规律了吗。

1428
00:52:26.190 --> 00:52:27.690
What's going to happen season two?
第二季会发生什么呢？

1429
00:52:27.910 --> 00:52:30.330
Who do I get stuck with in season two?
第二季我会和谁被困在一起？

1430
00:52:30.890 --> 00:52:31.470
Dun, dun, dun.
当当当。

1431
00:52:36.130 --> 00:52:38.710
Thank you for listening to Office Ladies Second Drink.
感谢收听《办公室女士》第二杯。

